      "example_skel": {
        "steps": [
          "Because \\(b^2>0\\), the equation implies that \\(a\\) and \\(\\log_{10}b\\) have the same sign. ",
          "If \\(a>0\\), then \\(b>1\\), and\n",
          "\\[\na=\\frac{\\log_{10}b}{b^2}.\n\\]\n",
          "For \\(b>1\\), \\(0<\\ln b<b-1\\) and \\(\\ln 10>1\\), so\n",
          "\\[\n0<a=\\frac{\\ln b}{(\\ln 10)b^2}<\\frac{b-1}{b^2}<1,\n\\]\n",
          "contradicting that \\(a\\) is a positive integer. ",
          "Also \\(b=1\\) would force \\(a=0\\), which is excluded. ",
          "Therefore \\(a<0\\) and \\(0<b<1\\). ",
          "The five values are ordered\n",
          "\\[\na<0<b<1<\\frac1b,\n\\]\n",
          "so their median is \\(\\boxed{b}.\\)"
        ],
